   <p>TEL AVIV, Israel — The Israeli military has launched what it called a "limited, localized" ground offensive in southern Lebanon against the Iran-backed Lebanese militant group Hezbollah.</p>   <p>"These targets are located in villages close to the border and pose an immediate threat to Israeli communities in northern Israel," the Israeli military <a href="https://x.com/IDF/status/1840890054819864776">said on social media</a> late Monday.</p>   <p>It said the Israeli air force and artillery "are supporting the ground forces with precise strikes on military targets in the area."</p>   <div id="resg-s1-25635" class="bucketwrap image large">
            <div
    class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"
    data-crop-type=""
    style="
        --source-width: 4131;
        --source-height: 2754;
    "
>
        <picture>
