<!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5133463-101" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK MEDIAPROMO PRIMARY" -->
   <p>Tamir Hayman, who served as the head of Israel’s military intelligence directorate until 2021, said in an interview on Israeli Army Radio on Monday that Israel’s airstrikes in Lebanon had successfully knocked Hezbollah off balance.</p>   <div id="resnx-s1-5133463-102" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col ">
            <div class="bucket img">
                  <a class="imagewrap" id="featuredStackSquareImageg-s1-25348" href="https://www.npr.org/2024/09/29/g-s1-25348/israel-hezbollah-lebanon-hassan-nasrallah-timeline"  data-metrics-ga4='{"category":"recirculation","action":"story_recirculation_click","clickType":"inset box","clickUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2024\/09\/29\/g-s1-25348\/israel-hezbollah-lebanon-hassan-nasrallah-timeline"}' ><picture><source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-format="webp" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/webp" /><source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/jpeg" /><img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/3648x3648+912+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F79%2F8d%2F20ef19e74be789977e33a93175da%2Fgettyimages-2173686267.jpg" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" alt="A portrait of Hezbollah chief Hassan Nasrallah sits amid destruction in a area targeted overnight by Israeli airstrikes in Saksakiyeh on Sep. 26, 2024." loading="lazy" /></picture></a>         <div class="bucketblock">
                        <h3 class="slug"><a href="https://www.npr.org/series/1205445976/middle-east-crisis">Middle East conflict </a></h3>
