   </div>

<!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5133463-102" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " -->
   <p>But he said Israel should think through the purpose of a ground invasion: Is it to create a permanent security buffer zone that Israel would occupy long term, with much international opposition, or only to remain temporarily to destroy Hezbollah infrastructure?</p>   <div id="resnx-s1-5133463-103" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col ">
            <div class="bucket img">
                  <a class="imagewrap" id="featuredStackSquareImageg-s1-25396" href="https://www.npr.org/2024/09/30/g-s1-25396/israel-beirut-lebanon-hezbollah"  data-metrics-ga4='{"category":"recirculation","action":"story_recirculation_click","clickType":"inset box","clickUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2024\/09\/30\/g-s1-25396\/israel-beirut-lebanon-hezbollah"}' ><picture><source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5760x5760+1440+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F24%2F04%2F4c2747bd43a8b3762bd452b57c02%2Fap24274020030360.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5760x5760+1440+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F24%2F04%2F4c2747bd43a8b3762bd452b57c02%2Fap24274020030360.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5760x5760+1440+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F24%2F04%2F4c2747bd43a8b3762bd452b57c02%2Fap24274020030360.jpg" data-format="webp" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/webp" /><source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5760x5760+1440+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F24%2F04%2F4c2747bd43a8b3762bd452b57c02%2Fap24274020030360.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5760x5760+1440+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F24%2F04%2F4c2747bd43a8b3762bd452b57c02%2Fap24274020030360.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5760x5760+1440+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F24%2F04%2F4c2747bd43a8b3762bd452b57c02%2Fap24274020030360.jpg" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/jpeg" /><img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5760x5760+1440+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F24%2F04%2F4c2747bd43a8b3762bd452b57c02%2Fap24274020030360.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5760x5760+1440+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F24%2F04%2F4c2747bd43a8b3762bd452b57c02%2Fap24274020030360.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/5760x5760+1440+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F24%2F04%2F4c2747bd43a8b3762bd452b57c02%2Fap24274020030360.jpg" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" alt="A fire engine ladder extends up a building that was hit in an apparent Israeli airstrike, in central Beirut early Monday, Sept. 30, 2024." loading="lazy" /></picture></a>         <div class="bucketblock">
                        <h3 class="slug"><a href="https://www.npr.org/series/1205445976/middle-east-crisis">Middle East conflict </a></h3>
            <h3><a href="https://www.npr.org/2024/09/30/g-s1-25396/israel-beirut-lebanon-hezbollah"  data-metrics-ga4='{"category":"recirculation","action":"story_recirculation_click","clickType":"inset box","clickUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2024\/09\/30\/g-s1-25396\/israel-beirut-lebanon-hezbollah"}' >An airstrike hits a Beirut residential building as Israel expands attacks in Lebanon</a></h3>
         </div>

<!-- END CLASS="BUCKETBLOCK" -->
      </div>

<!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" -->
   </div>

<!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5133463-103" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " -->
   <p>“Are we there in order to reach a deal and then leaving? Are we there in order to stay?” Hayman said.<br></p>   <h3 class="edTag">The U.S. is sending additional forces to the region</h3>   <p>The senior U.S. official told NPR that the Pentagon will send a “few thousand” more troops to the Middle East, focused on air defense capabilities.</p>   <p>The U.S. is concerned about retaliation to Israel’s moves by Iran and Iranian-supported militias in the region. Such a retaliation could threaten U.S. troops in Iraq and Syria.</p>   <div id="resnx-s1-5133463-104" class="bucketwrap statichtml">
            <div style="max-width: 650px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">

<p data-pym-loader data-child-src="https://apps.npr.org/datawrapper/WhH6c/2/" id="responsive-embed-WhH6c">Loading...</p>
<script src="https://pym.nprapps.org/npr-pym-loader.v2.min.js"></script>

</div>
   </div>

<!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5133463-104" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP STATICHTML" -->
   <h3 class="edTag">Israel’s strikes in Yemen offer a message to Iran</h3>   <p>Israel’s conflict with the Iran-backed Houthis in Yemen is also intensifying.</p>   <p>On Saturday, the Houthis, the main military group in Yemen, launched a ballistic missile toward central Israel, saying it was targeting Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s airplane returning from addressing the United Nations General Assembly in New York.</p>   <div id="resnx-s1-5133463-105" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col ">
            <div class="bucket img">
                  <a class="imagewrap" id="featuredStackSquareImageg-s1-25343" href="https://www.npr.org/2024/09/29/g-s1-25343/pentagon-iran-hezbollah-israel-middle-east"  data-metrics-ga4='{"category":"recirculation","action":"story_recirculation_click","clickType":"inset box","clickUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2024\/09\/29\/g-s1-25343\/pentagon-iran-hezbollah-israel-middle-east"}' ><picture><source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/683x683+171+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F98%2Fa2%2Fa0613685435abbc0673754f4813f%2Fgettyimages-2165602692.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/683x683+171+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F98%2Fa2%2Fa0613685435abbc0673754f4813f%2Fgettyimages-2165602692.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/683x683+171+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F98%2Fa2%2Fa0613685435abbc0673754f4813f%2Fgettyimages-2165602692.jpg" data-format="webp" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/webp" /><source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/683x683+171+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F98%2Fa2%2Fa0613685435abbc0673754f4813f%2Fgettyimages-2165602692.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/683x683+171+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F98%2Fa2%2Fa0613685435abbc0673754f4813f%2Fgettyimages-2165602692.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/683x683+171+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F98%2Fa2%2Fa0613685435abbc0673754f4813f%2Fgettyimages-2165602692.jpg" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" type="image/jpeg" /><img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/683x683+171+0/resize/100/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F98%2Fa2%2Fa0613685435abbc0673754f4813f%2Fgettyimages-2165602692.jpg" data-original="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/683x683+171+0/resize/100/quality/100/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F98%2Fa2%2Fa0613685435abbc0673754f4813f%2Fgettyimages-2165602692.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/683x683+171+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F98%2Fa2%2Fa0613685435abbc0673754f4813f%2Fgettyimages-2165602692.jpg" data-format="jpeg" class="img lazyOnLoad" alt="Secretary of Defense Lloyd Austin is pictured at the U.S. Naval Academy on Aug. 6 in Annapolis, Md. " loading="lazy" /></picture></a>         <div class="bucketblock">
                        <h3 class="slug"><a href="https://www.npr.org/sections/world/">World </a></h3>
            <h3><a href="https://www.npr.org/2024/09/29/g-s1-25343/pentagon-iran-hezbollah-israel-middle-east"  data-metrics-ga4='{"category":"recirculation","action":"story_recirculation_click","clickType":"inset box","clickUrl":"https:\/\/www.npr.org\/2024\/09\/29\/g-s1-25343\/pentagon-iran-hezbollah-israel-middle-east"}' >The Pentagon says it wants to prevent Iran from spreading the conflict in the Middle East</a></h3>
         </div>

<!-- END CLASS="BUCKETBLOCK" -->
      </div>

<!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" -->
   </div>

<!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5133463-105" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " -->
   <p>Netanyahu landed in Israel shortly before air raid sirens wailed at the airport and throughout central Israel. The Israeli military said it intercepted the missile midair.</p>   <p>On Sunday, Israel’s military said it sent dozens of fighter jets and refueling aircraft more than 1,000 miles away to Yemen, where it said it bombed power plants and a seaport used by the Houthis to import oil for military purposes. The Houthis said the areas hit were civilian targets and that at least four people were killed and dozens wounded in the Israeli strikes.</p>   <p>Israeli security analysts said Israel’s bombing campaign in Yemen was a message to Iran, showing Israel’s long-range flight capability as a tacit warning to Iran that it, too, was within Israel’s reach.</p>   <aside id="ad-third-wrap" class="ad-wrap third" aria-label="advertisement">
    <div class="ad-header "><span>Sponsor Message</span></div>

    <div class="ad-config-wrap">
      <div id="ad-third-News_World_Middle_East" class="ad-config ad-third has-refresh-enabled" data-ad-config='{"network":"\/6735\/","zone":"News_World_Middle_East","targets":{"testserver":"false","isPodcastEpisode":"false","storyId":"nx-s1-5133463","agg":["1205445976","1046346178"]},"site":{"desktop":"NPRThird","mobile":"NPRMobileThird"},"location":"third","deferred":false,"isBetweenContent":true,"hasRefreshEnabled":true,"isOutstreamVideoEnabled":false}'>
        <div style="min-height:90px"></div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <div class="ad-footer "></div>
</aside>
   <p><em>This is a developing story that may be updated.</em></p>   <p><em>Daniel Estrin reported from Tel Aviv, Israel; Alex Leff from Washington, D.C. Jane Arraf contributed reporting from Beirut and Tom Bowman contributed reporting from Washington. </em></p>
</div>
